From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Onyx contributors <onyx@localhost>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:33:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/17] The curl network back end and PAL's digests on mbedTLS
 (USE(MBEDTLS))

What:
- platform/network/curl/CurlTLSBackend.h: the TLS library as the curl back end sees it (the
  connection type CURLINFO_TLS_SSL_PTR gives, curl's back-end id, a namespace TLSHelper) for
  OpenSSL or mbedTLS; CurlContext, CurlSSLVerifier, CertificateInfoCurl use it instead of naming
  OpenSSL.
- MbedTLSHelper.{h,cpp}: the counterpart of OpenSSLHelper on an mbedtls_ssl_context: the peer's
  chain as PEM, the certificate summary (subject CN / O, validity, the DNS and IP alternative
  names), the verification flags and their description, the TLS version and ciphersuite.
- CurlSSLVerifier: with mbedTLS nothing is installed on the configuration curl hands over (curl
  has its own verification callback there); the chain and the verification result are read from
  the connection after the handshake. CurlSSLHandle.h: no <openssl/crypto.h>.
- Curl.cmake: OpenSSLHelper / OpenSSL::SSL or MbedTLSHelper / MbedTLS::mbedtls by USE_MBEDTLS;
  PublicSuffixStoreCurl and libpsl only when the port has libpsl.
- PAL: crypto/mbedtls/CryptoDigestMbedTLS.cpp (SHA-1 / 256 / 384 / 512 on mbedtls_md).

Why: Onyx's curl is built with mbedTLS (the system's TLS library); there is no OpenSSL. curl's
mbedTLS back end gives what WebKit needs (CURLOPT_SSL_CTX_FUNCTION, CURLINFO_TLS_SSL_PTR).
